# Sanitize Last, Always

Ordering is the whole design. Sanitization is not a step in the pipeline; it is the
door out of it.

## Why order matters

A rewrite that runs *after* the allowlist can introduce anything it likes. A rewrite
that runs before it is checked like everything else, including a route returned by
an injected mapping the renderer does not control.

## Determinism

Identical input must produce byte-identical output. That sounds obvious until a
syntax highlighter with a process-wide grammar registry renders the same fence two
different ways depending on which page was built first.

```javascript
/** Settle the registry once, before any render reads it. */
const ready = load(modifiers);
export const render = async (source) => {
  await ready;
  return highlight(source);
};
```

